Hi Michelle,

I went through the combined rehearsal idea from your deck. We need separate d=
ay and night windows at the single site. If both are put into the same slot, =
the night team cannot check its own handoff. Having the day contact there doe=
s not establish that the night handoff works.

The attached load starts after Janet has coordinated the initial roster and s=
ite contacts. At the end of week 4 we can show the reconciled recipients, the=
 single-site rehearsal results and the issue list, not a full move onto regul=
ar shifts. The responsible JDH contact still needs to approve the corrections=
 before the first live group.

Weeks 2 and 4 each use all 28 available hours. There are 116 demand hours in =
weeks 5=E2=80=939; moving them into the first four weeks would also put corre=
ctions, approval and cutovers ahead of the work they depend on. The nine week=
s are an estimate, not booked dates.

Thanks,
Divya

